<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Collegio (Venice)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pien Collegio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Collegio, or Full College (Pien Collegio), was the steering committee of the government of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. It brought together the doge, his six councillors, the heads of the criminal court and the boards of savi (sages) responsible for policy, war and the mainland. It received ambassadors, read dispatches and prepared business for the Senate, meeting in its own hall in the Doge's Palace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/collegio-venice.jpg" alt="Collegio (Venice)" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Malombra · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pietro_Malombra_Audience_of_the_Spanish_ambassador_in_Venice.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
